 Mean: Unknown Population Variance"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c96b7a75-2013-5c7f-b88e-9d3588d462dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168976} {:answer/id #uuid "067cb327-4b43-59e7-a52c-c7902b4f4c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168977} {:answer/id #uuid "47c5d296-7085-51aa-a56c-ded04a116db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168978} {:answer/id #uuid "5c36b2ab-527e-5abd-97f7-5476740857df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168979} {:answer/id #uuid "770a5405-bedd-5f3a-9c5e-bf90963a0b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168980}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ac706d58-8e8c-5ac9-b7e0-fed5d21aa411" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168975}] :question/id #uuid "c3be7a5b-3b7a-59cd-ba4c-2dfe8d8cae37" :question/math-academy-id "q-159355" :question/problem "Consider a sample of size $n = 24$ from a normal population. We wish to carry out a hypothesis test at the $10%$ level of significance to determine whether there is sufficient evidence that the population mean $μ$ does not equal $30$.\n\nGiven that the mean of the sample is $x^(―) = 32$ and the sample standard deviation $s = 4$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The **two-tailed** critical region for the test statistic is approximately $T \\le - 2.492$ or $T \\ge 2.492$\n2. At the $10%$ level of significance, there is **insufficient** evidence that $μ \\ne 30$\n3. At the $10%$ level of significance, there is **sufficient** evidence that $μ \\ne 30$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution $T_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores $t_{k, p}$ such that $P(T > t_{k, p}) = p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p$.*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $23$ | $1.319$ | $1.714$ | $2.069$ | $2.500$ | $2.807$ |\n| $24$ | $1.318$ | $1.711$ | $2.064$ | $2.492$ | $2.797$ |\n| $25$ | $1.316$ | $1.708$ | $2.060$ | $2.485$ | $2.787$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172127 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37781e6c-9598-547b-b5c6-8296a7daf3b2" :knowledge-point/title "Testing a Hypothesis for a Large Sample" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049921 :topic/math-academy-id 3311 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for One Mean: Unknown Population Variance"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afcc5588-1d2a-531d-8a6f-bba6f4c50ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168982} {:answer/id #uuid "c75b0320-cf93-54b4-bdeb-28bb798e2425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168983} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e38411-431f-5e79-9fbc-b4523b2237df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168984} {:answer/id #uuid "f2dd95bd-ffd7-5d77-92b4-ed9c0cd818b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168985} {:answer/id #uuid "2725188b-028e-54b8-b1d2-dcc0de31c85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :