 Mean: Unknown Population Variance"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a676e56-58d9-5625-b1ed-99758b980692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168988} {:answer/id #uuid "cd36827f-a8a1-57c9-bc49-4db2447cc35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168989} {:answer/id #uuid "23ec8775-957f-532e-ba1d-c52083ec0b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168990} {:answer/id #uuid "52745147-dc46-5b78-bc15-7f18e3ed3777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168991} {:answer/id #uuid "707680bb-a9f9-5e92-8181-ed661f630771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168992}] :answer-field/id #uuid "389de89f-a8fe-5830-9d0f-19b402d1c96b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168987}] :question/id #uuid "12cc79ca-f537-5d2a-b5af-96ac4e611603" :question/math-academy-id "q-159360" :question/problem "After collecting data over several years, a farmer knows that the mean weight of the apples in their harvest each year is normally distributed with mean $μ = 140g$. This year, the farmer decided to use a different fertilizer, and they want to know whether the mean weight of the apples in the harvest this year is larger than $140g$. They decide to conduct a hypothesis test at the $5%$ significance level.\n\nGiven that the farmer sampled $24$ apples from the harvest and found that their sample mean weight is $144g$ and the sample standard deviation is $s = 20g$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The critical regi