 and $Y$ with standard deviations $σ_{x} = 2$ and $σ_{y} = 1$, respectively. We wish to carry out the hypothesis test at the $1%$ significance level to determine whether there is sufficient evidence that the population mean $μ_{x}$ of $X$ is smaller than the population mean $μ_{y}$ of $Y$.\n\nGiven that the sample means are $x^(―) = 2$ and $y^(―) = 3$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The $1%$ **one-tailed** critical region for the test statistic is approximately $Z \\le - 2.326$\n2. At the $1%$ level of significance, there is **insufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} < μ_{y}$\n3. At the $1%$ level of significance, there is **sufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} < μ_{y}$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172124 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "46341011-0c5c-5237-b7b8-ef63b661bc05" :knowledge-point/title "Applications of Hypothesis Testing" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049154 :topic/math-academy-id 3310 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for Two Means: Known Population Variances"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c626cea-cdc5-57d2-b7d7-0f8cdbcb478b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169006} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e7e3cd-3118-54cd-93dc-0c9360632417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169007} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1d1c61-b053-5f83-8987-46160e166f30" :answ