 $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172124 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "46341011-0c5c-5237-b7b8-ef63b661bc05" :knowledge-point/title "Applications of Hypothesis Testing" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049154 :topic/math-academy-id 3310 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for Two Means: Known Population Variances"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c2bd94-fbe5-55b4-a194-1b679ab22cc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169012} {:answer/id #uuid "ac177538-7abe-5fb9-80c9-c5a4bf09074d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169013} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0c8e70-3a4f-5082-b5ad-4cf9643064e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169014} {:answer/id #uuid "ef23a664-19f3-596d-8a73-f6e8368490b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169015} {:answer/id #uuid "089d7df3-7ab1-5e02-af91-8f8c986d725c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169016}] :answer-field/id #uuid "08bb260a-a276-53f8-9393-ba0ff6e8147c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169011}] :question/id #uuid "14900240-c896-52b9-96d8-92807fa245a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-159378" :question/problem "Previous studies show that the scores of girls and boys on a particular test for dyslexia have standard deviations of $2$ points and $3$ points, respectively. Scientists want to determine whether the population mean $μ_{x}$ for girls is the same as the population mean $μ_{y}$ for boys. They decide to conduct a hypothesis test at the $1%$ significance level.\n\nGiven that the scientists sampled $125$ girls and $118$ boys and found that their mean scores on the test are $42$ points and $41$ points, respectively, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The $1%$ critical region for the test statistic is approximately $Z \\le - 2.576$ or $Z \\ge 2.576$\n2. At the $1%$ level of significance, there is **insufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} \\ne μ_{y}$\n3. At the $1%$ level of significance, there is **sufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} \\ne μ_{y}$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172116 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67425653-1c20-5713-b2cb-5569c26c2cf9" :knowledge-point/title "Testing a Hypothesis Given a Normal Population: One-Tailed Tests" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050729 :topic/math-academy-id 3303 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for One Mean: Known Population Variance"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2c369f4-f0bf-53cb-87ec-4910a42618f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169018} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf40101-835f-5334-baeb-1f0f8133288c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169019} {:answer/id #uuid "1