282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be6d2ce2-f7cc-5a87-86d1-21f769dbd580" :knowledge-point/title "Applications of Confidence Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049866 :topic/math-academy-id 3298 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Two Means: Known and Unequal Population Variances"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2465302-e38b-5022-97f1-e3508fe38200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169078} {:answer/id #uuid "e45a9763-7472-5249-8d87-0217a4f64059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169079} {:answer/id #uuid "655be236-db0f-5619-97b4-155d41b0cc52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169080} {:answer/id #uuid "66f7c51b-3ded-581d-bd3f-c423369d6bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169081} {:answer/id #uuid "7d26245b-397f-5b69-8629-5b522cf34b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169082}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9c93f752-af6d-5f66-b0e2-647fec3249d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169077}] :question/id #uuid "e988df3e-2b97-5c9e-988c-9ed264a72932" :question/math-academy-id "q-159507" :question/problem "The scores on the final calculus test in states X and Y are known to be normally distributed with standard deviations of $σ_{x} = 5$ points and $σ_{y} = 4$ points, respectively. Scientists want to determine whether the population mean $μ_{x}$ of scores in state X is smaller than the population mean of scores in state Y. They decide to construct a $90%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population means.\n\nThe scientists sampled $35$ students from state X and $23$ students from state Y, finding that their mean scores are $85$ points and $87$ points, respectively. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The end-points of the $90%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population means are approximately $-2 ± 2.105$.\n2. All values contained within the $90%$ confidence interval are negative.\n3. The confidence interval data suggests that $μ_{x} < μ_{y}$.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172129 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be6d2ce2-f7cc-5a87-86d1-21f769dbd580" :knowledge-point/title "Applications of Confidence Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049866 :topic/math-academy-id 3298 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Two Means: Known and Unequal Population Variances"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa81f763-d71e-55a8-bbff-21322b0f02ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186169084} {:answer/id #uuid "c5edff8e-8184-5105-b9b7-17b0972a2a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answe