ne μ_{y}$\n3. At the $1%$ level of significance, there is **sufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} \\ne μ_{y}$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution $T_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores $t_{k, p}$ such that $P(T > t_{k, p}) = p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p$.*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $43$ | $1.302$ | $1.681$ | $2.017$ | $2.416$ | $2.695$ |\n| $44$ | $1.301$ | $1.680$ | $2.015$ | $2.414$ | $2.692$ |\n| $45$ | $1.301$ | $1.679$ | $2.014$ | $2.412$ | $2.690$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171968 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c62ddd95-c0e5-5125-8e7a-7bda55e333db" :knowledge-point/title "Testing a Hypothesis Given Large Samples" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048509 :topic/math-academy-id 3313 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for Two Means: Equal But Unknown Population Variances"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6009bd7-04c3-5d8a-aae2-e433a11ff7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170472} {:answer/id #uuid "212910e2-bd2b-5c44-b9b7-ecfd89aab948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170473} {:answer/id #uuid "29307f34-a9a4-57e4-9062-dbf37f36d00f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170474} {:answer/id #uuid "327db5bc-a92c-577f-86c4-629ca9ce785b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170475} {:answer/id #uuid "7e399853-553a-5eda-9c96-14c0827bb531" :ans